note Table accesses are written inline, `get a_ar add get a_rb R i` / `put a_ar add get a_rb R i v`,
note checked only by a_ar's own length: every index is in its region by construction. A count
note grows only after a_need has given its group room for it, reads use indices below a count, links
note omc stored (each below a count) or hash buckets below the bucket count, and input bytes are read
note from region 0 at word 0, padded with 64 zero bytes (a_rdin). The lines whose registers did not
note fit inline use the calls below; a_g / a_gu / a_p check the region (a_oob, trap 3), as a_pc,
note a_bput and a_ib do. gate-nocaps, gate12 and gate-usage drive every group far past its first room.
note The argument holds only when the count that bounds an index is the count of the region's own group:
note rscan once read the calls (group 9) at an inline edge's index (group 17), past them once the edges
note outnumbered the calls' room (trap 3, omc c52e986e and 1e628c80). gate-nocaps step 4 compiles a unit
note past every group's first room with a checked twin of this file (each inline access the checked call).
fn a_g r ulong i ulong to ulong
if ge i get a_rw r
a_oob i
end
ret get a_ar add get a_rb r i
end

fn a_gu r ulong i ulong to uchar
if ge i get a_rw r
a_oob i
end
ret uchar get a_ar add get a_rb r i
end

fn a_p r ulong i ulong v ulong to void
if ge i get a_rw r
a_oob i
end
put a_ar add get a_rb r i v
end


note mflush: complete a diagnostic/query stdout chunk or report compiler output error 2.
fn mflush to void
off = ulong 0
n = get mc 0
while lt off n
w = write 1 msg off sub n off
if le w 0
if ne get d2mode 0 0
note d2site 623|mflush: standard output refused a diagnostic or query chunk
put d2site 0 623
fail 2
end
exit int 2
end
off = add off ulong w
end
put mc 0 0
end

fn mputb b uchar to void
m = get mc 0
put msg m b
put mc 0 add m 1
end

fn mputn v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
i = ulong 0
x = v
put d 0 uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
i = add i 1
while gt x 0
put d i uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
i = add i 1
end
j = i
while gt j 0
j = sub j 1
mputb get d j
end
end

note fail: write "omc: line N: error E" to stderr (fd 2) and exit with the code
fn fail code ulong to void
put mc 0 0
mputb 111
mputb 109
mputb 99
mputb 58
mputb 32
mputb 108
mputb 105
mputb 110
mputb 101
mputb 32
mputn add get line 0 get lbase 0
mputb 58
mputb 32
mputb 101
mputb 114
mputb 114
mputb 111
mputb 114
mputb 32
mputn code
if ne get d2mode 0 0
mputb 58
mputb 32
d2mean code
mputb 59
mputb 32
d2reason
end
mputb 10
w = write 2 msg 0 get mc 0
if ne get om2 0 0
if eq get om2m 0 1
drec code
end
end
if and ge get chkmode 0 1 le get chkmode 0 2
note A stdout failure cannot report another record to stdout.
if ne code 2
diagrec code
end
end
if ne get d2mode 0 0
d2record code
end
note An arena-full error 14, and any error of a usage unit, ends with the omc-use record (a_rec).
if or ne get a_fl 0 0 eq get chkmode 0 3
a_rec 2
end
exit int code
end

note mputw: the first n bytes (at most 8) of the little-endian packed word w
fn mputw w ulong n ulong to void
i = ulong 0
x = w
while lt i n
mputb uchar and x 255
x = shr x 8
i = add i 1
end
end

note dcol: the 1-based column of byte a in its line
fn dcol a ulong to ulong
j = a
go = true
while go
m = ulong 0
while and go lt m 999999
if eq j 0
go = false
else
if eq a_ib sub j 1 10
go = false
else
j = sub j 1
end
end
m = add m 1
end
end
ret add sub a j 1
end

note dsev_w: sev= incomplete when the failure is on the end-of-input token (or inside a text literal cut by
note the end), unknown for an undeclared function or struct, else error
fn dsev_w code ulong to void
s = get dsev 0
if eq s 0
if eq get tk 0 3
s = ulong 1
end
if and eq code 22 ge get cur 0 get inlen 0
s = ulong 1
end
end
if eq s 1
mputw 7308339910638005865 8
mputw 25972 2
ret
end
if eq s 2
mputw 31093567915781749 7
ret
end
mputw 491496043109 5
end

note dexp_w: expect= the class of token being read (end for an open function at the end of the input)
fn dexp_w code ulong to void
e = get dexp 0
if eq code 15
e = ulong 5
end
if or eq code 6 eq code 8
e = ulong 4
end
if eq e 1
mputw 435761734006 5
ret
end
if eq e 2
mputw 1701869940 4
ret
end
if eq e 3
mputw 1701667182 4
ret
end
if eq e 4
mputw 125779768604014 6
ret
end
if eq e 5
mputw 6581861 3
ret
end
if eq e 6
mputw 28550371718161774 7
ret
end
mputw 1685221239 4
end

note dobl_w: obligation= from the code: 27 init, 28 ctor, 29 layout, 21 bounds, 14 growth, 12 regs, else -
fn dobl_w code ulong to void
if eq code 30
mputw 8386654075301556067 8
ret
end
if eq code 27
mputw 1953066601 4
ret
end
if eq code 28
mputw 1919906915 4
