note fmtbyte: one input byte of the canonical text. fst: 0 line start, 1 indentation (kept, dropped
note again on a blank line), 2 note line (copied), 3 between words, 4 in a word, 5 in a text literal, 6
note after a backslash in a text literal. A run of blanks between words (fpend, starting at output byte
note fbo) is written as it comes, then becomes one space unless a parenthesis is next to it (fprp: the
note word before it was one); at the end of the line it is dropped.
fn fmtbyte p ulong to void
b = uchar and shr get a_ar shr p 3 shl and p 7 3 255
s = get fst 0
if eq b 10
if lt s 2
put oc 0 get flso 0
else
if ne get fpend 0 0
put oc 0 get fbo 0
end
end
emitb 10
put fst 0 0
put fpend 0 0
put fprp 0 0
put flso 0 get oc 0
ret
end
if eq s 2
emitb b
ret
end
if eq s 5
emitb b
if eq b 92
put fst 0 6
end
if eq b 34
put fst 0 3
put fprp 0 0
end
ret
end
if eq s 6
emitb b
put fst 0 5
ret
end
blank = or eq b 32 eq b 9
if lt s 2
if blank
emitb b
put fst 0 1
ret
end
if ne isnote p 0
emitb b
put fst 0 2
ret
end
put fst 0 3
put fpend 0 0
end
if blank
if eq get fpend 0 0
put fbo 0 get oc 0
put fpend 0 1
end
emitb b
put fst 0 3
ret
end
paren = or eq b 40 eq b 41
if and eq get fst 0 4 not paren
emitb b
ret
end
if ne get fpend 0 0
if and eq get fprp 0 0 not paren
put oc 0 get fbo 0
emitb 32
end
end
put fpend 0 0
emitb b
if eq b 34
put fst 0 5
put fprp 0 0
ret
end
if paren
put fst 0 3
put fprp 0 1
else
put fst 0 4
put fprp 0 0
end
end

fn fmtout to void
put oc 0 0
put fst 0 0
put fpend 0 0
put fprp 0 0
put flso 0 0
e = get inlen 0
p = ulong 0
go = true
while go
m = ulong 0
while and go lt m 999999
if ge p e
go = false
else
fmtbyte p
p = add p 1
end
m = add m 1
end
end
if ge get fst 0 2
if ne get fpend 0 0
put oc 0 get fbo 0
end
emitb 10
end
put fmtm 0 0
put om2m 0 0
writeout 0
end

note tok_hex (OM-2): 0x and 1..16 digits 0-9 a-f is the unsigned value (tk 2, tbig as tok_num). A - before
