st = get oc 0
emit or 3531603969 shl code 5
back tail
end
patch19 a_g 44 j st
end
j = add j 1
end
m = add m 1
end
end
code = add code 1
end
end

note island: a B.cond reaches 1 MiB (19-bit word field), and a function's stubs used to sit only at its
note end. When the oldest site no stub was patched to yet is 512 KiB back, B over a group of stubs here
note and patch the waiting sites to it (stubs), so a function of any length keeps every trap branch in
note reach. Only between lines of a function body (stmt: AArch64, not IR mode, no open inline frame, so
note never inside a contract's evaluation, which may expand an inline function and then erase its code)
note and outside every if, else, while and for (open unrolled bodies only, which no branch spans): an
note island never lengthens a block, so every block keeps the branch spans it had (an if or loop body over
note 1 MiB stays error 24, as before). A function whose sites never wait that long compiles as before.
fn island to void
p = get tpend 0
n = get nt 0
if ge p n
ret
end
if lt sub get oc 0 get a_ar add get a_rb 44 p 524288
ret
end
i = ulong 0
go = true
while go
m = ulong 0
while and go lt m 999999
if ge i get nb 0
go = false
else
k = get a_ar add get a_rb 49 i
if and ge k 1 le k 4
ret
end
i = add i 1
end
m = add m 1
end
end
bo = get oc 0
emit 335544320
stubs p n
patch26 bo get oc 0
put tpend 0 n
end

note patchl: patch to t every entry of loop i in the break (w 0) or continue (w 1) list, from the list's
note count when loop i opened (bk0 / bc0) to its end
fn patchl w ulong i ulong t ulong to void
