note OP12 general file (new): ARG sub bits0..7, volume bits8..15 (255 = the volume this image was
note loaded from), position bits16..63. Open subs take the path A[OFF..OFF+N): 1..255 bytes, first
note '\', each 32..126. Sub 0 open read-only, 5 open an existing file read/write (no truncate), both
note result FileSize; 1 create empty, replacing any file (result 0). Sub 2 reads up to N bytes at
note the position into A (result bytes read, 0 at end), 3 writes N bytes there (result N; needs sub
note 1 or 5), 4 flushes and closes (result 0). One file at a time: its handle stays in private 2304
note and its volume root in 2312 between operations. Errors: 32 sub, 33 path, 34 busy, 35 nothing
note open, 36 open/create/delete, 37 read, 38 write (or not writable), 39 short write, 40 flush,
note 41 GetInfo; volume errors 16..22 as efi 11. Refusals 32..35 and 38 not-writable leave the slot
note as it was (the caller still owns an open file); so do the firmware errors 37, 38 and 39 of subs
note 2 and 3. Volume errors leave the slot empty. 36 and 41 close the file and root, slot empty;
note sub 4 with a file open closes both and empties the slot on every path, returning 40 when Flush
note failed. A file still open at exit is flushed and closed by the shared exit (xefx 1).
