note ======== a64efi: UEFI AArch64 PE32+ application (docs/A64-EFI.md) ========
note The default AArch64 code generator with three differences: addresses are base-relative (mataddr),
note every exit branches to the shared firmware return at file offset 520 (aefx), and there are no host
note words. Private state is the first 16 KiB of the .bss, whose base stays in X27: 0 ImageHandle,
note 8 SystemTable, 16..111 X19..X30, 112 the firmware SP, 120..183 D8..D15 (AAPCS64 callee-saved, UEFI
note 2.10 2.3.6), 184 the address of fn efiexit when the program has one, 192 the status across it.
note The Omega stack is the rest of the first 8 MiB (X28 = base + 16 KiB), the globals follow.

note aefx: the shared return, X0 = EFI_STATUS. When slot 184 holds a function it is called once on a
note fresh stack (the slot is cleared first, so a trap inside it returns), then the callee-saved
note registers and the firmware stack come back and RET returns to the firmware.
