note aret: the result of a firmware word, X0 as a ulong, after the saved registers come back
fn aret dst ulong x ulong to void
sl = get a_ar add get a_rb 77 add x 7
r = restore dst sl get svn 0 get sva 0 1
vdone 1 r 5
end

note aefival: efi OP ARG A OFF N -> ulong, the contract of x86efi's word. OP is a literal 0..14, A writable
note uchar storage with OFF + N inside it (trap 3). Here the operation is Omega code: the word is a call of
note the program's own fn efirt op arg addr n (four ulong, result ulong), which must be defined above its
note first use (error 16) and reaches the firmware through the fw words.
