note afw: the firmware words, all ulong in and out. They carry raw addresses, which no other word does:
note fwcall F A0 A1 A2 A3 A4 A5: BLR F with A0..A5 in X0..X5 (AAPCS64), result X0; 64 KiB of stack must
note   be free (trap 6). fwld ADDR W / fwst ADDR W V: load or store W = 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes (another W is 1) at
note ADDR; fwst gives 0. fwsys K: 0 ImageHandle, 1 SystemTable, 2 CNTVCT_EL0 after ISB, 3 CNTFRQ_EL0, else
note MIDR_EL1. fwadr A OFF N: the address of A[OFF], with OFF + N inside A (trap 3).
